<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8060" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεγ-είρω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wake up, rouse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ὕπνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.138
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκλεχέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.730
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀηδόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					208
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				1055
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηγέρθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					3.1.12
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.257
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>): poet. aor.
			
				Med.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεγρόμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.522
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναέγρετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Maiist.
					31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>wake up, raise,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					8(7).2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολπήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					370
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεγειρομένα φάμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					4(3).23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. also,
				<i>rouse, encourage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέγειρα δ᾽ ἑταίρους μειλιχίοις
					ἐπέεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.172
				</span></i>
			; <i>stir, rouse the spirit of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμοειδῆ ἵππον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					9.6
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>take heart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.120
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of
			buildings, <i>raise,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.693a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				11.56
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ θεμελίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					422
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Judaea</span>).</div>
